{
   "id": "ITM-AGT-10009-01",
   "archetype_id": "BC-QA-10009",
   "variant_id": null,
   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A function \\( f \\) has derivatives of all orders. The second-degree Taylor polynomial for \\( f \\) about \\( x = 1 \\) is used to approximate \\( f\\left(\\frac{6}{5}\\right) \\). It is known that \\( f'''(1) = 2 \\) and that \\( |f'''(x)| \\le 6 \\) for all \\( x \\) in \\( \\left[1, \\frac{6}{5}\\right] \\). Find the Lagrange error bound for this approximation."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         1,
         125
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 2 polynomial needs the maximum of \\( |f'''(x)| \\), the derivative of order \\( 3 \\), between the centre and the input.",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The bound is \\( \\frac{M\\,|x - 1|^{3}}{3!} \\) with \\( M = 6 \\) and \\( |x - 1| = \\frac{1}{5} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            125
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluating gives \\( \\frac{6 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^{3}}{6} = \\frac{1}{125} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            125
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The error is at most \\( \\frac{1}{125} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            125
         ]
      }
   ],
